      "Turn-flow example: Play begins with player to dealer's right and proceeds counterclockwise. On turn, play exactly one card from hand. If its rank matches the top of any table pile (central play pile or any capture pile), take that top card plus any immediately underlying equal-rank cards and place them on top of your capture pile. If no match exists, place played card on top of central play pile. After all players exhaust current 4-card hands, dealer gives another 4 to each if stock remains. Continue until stock and hands are empty.",
      'Scoring example: Number cards score 5 each, J/Q/K score 10 each, and Aces score 20 each from captured piles only. First player or team to reach or exceed agreed target total, usually 500 or 1000, wins..',
